{"chapter": "conventions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0005", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-remark-big-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60933e2eb73b5869424ecf69d90b96f339f85ff45ff143b7b9fe9b3e0ad8de56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:77437c9c6d3e9c7afbf8a50e302e30a617a975eea757e102606bc22f713da3a9", "source_text": "A category <MATH_0001> consists of a set of objects and, for each pair of objects, a set of morphisms between them. In other words, it is what is called a “small” category in other texts. We will use “big” categories (categories whose objects form a proper class) as well, but only those that are listed in Categories, Remark <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d79423fefad5d444137df5bc2ebb7be2d33c7d4cdd3f6f1adbc295bedb301ad3", "unit_id": "tag:0005:p001"}
